@startuml
' Figure 26.3  Client, server and transport in the tool protocol
' Reading order: top to bottom. The client discovers the server, lists
' tools, and calls one over the transport; authorization covers who
' may call. The gateway sits in the path and checks each call against
' the registry; the protocol itself does not.
!include plantuml-theme.puml
participant "Client\n(harness)" as C <<model>>
participant "Gateway" as G <<policy>>
participant "Server" as S <<ops>>
C -> G : Discover, token
G -> S : Discover
S --> C : Capabilities
C -> G : List tools
G -> G : Hash vs registry
G --> C : Reviewed tools only
C -> G : Call tool, arguments
G -> G : Scope, schema, policy
G -> S : Call
S --> C : Result, capped
@enduml
